sections.body:
Before paying for non-refundable arrangements, confirm:

- the entry policy is valid on your travel dates;
- your passport type and nationality are eligible;
- your travel purpose and length of stay are covered;
- a transit itinerary continues to a qualifying third destination;
- your entry port can process the policy you intend to use; and
- your accommodation details are ready for the arrival card and registration.

If one part is unclear, ask the Chinese embassy or consulate responsible for your place of residence, or contact the National Immigration Administration service line. A short official answer is worth more than several confident but outdated travel posts.
